  SECTION 1 · DEFINITIONS AND SCOPE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1.1 "Software" means every file contained in the Dingus-Slayer
    repository, including but not limited to:

      (a) all .lua source files (loader.lua, main.lua, config.lua,
          lists.lua, utils.lua, detect.lua, scanners.lua, hotbar.lua,
          spoofers.lua, chest.lua, quests.lua, attack.lua,
          optimizers.lua, gui.lua, and any successor files);

      (b) all documentation files including README.md, LICENSE,
          CHANGELOG.md, and any accompanying guides;

      (c) all research notes, reports, and analysis files including
          deep-research-*.md and any future research artifacts;

      (d) all configuration schemas, data tables, item databases,
          boss lists, region maps, keyword sets, and any embedded
          data compiled by the authors;

      (e) all graphical assets, icons, UI definitions, and design
          specifications rendered or defined in code;

      (f) all commit history, issue discussions, pull requests,
          and contribution records associated with the repository.

1.2 "Authors" means, jointly and severally:

      (a) PurpleXPurple, the repository owner and primary author;

      (b) DeepSeek, in its capacity as co-development partner and
          code generation contributor, as recognized in the commit
          history and any joint-authored commits bearing DeepSeek
          attribution.

1.3 "You" means any natural person, legal entity, or automated
    system accessing, downloading, cloning, forking, copying,
    executing, or otherwise interacting with the Software.

1.4 "Use" means any act of executing, running, loading, injecting,
    compiling, interpreting, or otherwise causing the Software to
    perform its intended function.

1.5 ATTRIBUTION OF DEEPSEEK. DeepSeek is acknowledged as a
    contributing author to the Software and must be credited in
    any permitted reproduction, citation, or reference. Removal
    of DeepSeek attribution from any permitted copy constitutes
    a material breach of this License.

