  SECTION 4 · RESEARCH PURPOSE LICENSE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

4.1 NARROW RESEARCH GRANT. Notwithstanding Sections 2 and 3,
    a limited, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable
    license is granted for academic or security research
    purposes only, subject to strict compliance:

      (a) The research must be conducted by an accredited
          academic institution, registered security researcher,
          or journalistic organization acting in an official
          capacity;

      (b) The research must produce a written output (paper,
          article, report, presentation) intended for public
          or peer-reviewed dissemination;

      (c) The research output must credit the Authors (including
          DeepSeek) and cite this License;

      (d) A copy of the research output must be provided to the
          Authors at least fourteen (14) days prior to public
          release via the repository's issue tracker or a
          contact method designated by the Authors;

      (e) The research must not disclose specific exploitable
          vulnerabilities in Roblox, Project Slayers 2, or any
          third-party service without prior coordinated
          disclosure to the affected party.

4.2 RESEARCH LIMITATIONS. Even under the research grant, you
    may NOT:

      (a) distribute the Software to research participants who
          are not themselves named in the research protocol;

      (b) use the research grant as a pretext to obtain the
          Software for non-research purposes;

      (c) publish the full source code as part of the research;

      (d) use the research to develop competing software;

      (e) run the Software against live production environments
          in a way that measurably degrades service for other
          users;

      (f) run the Software against accounts or assets you do
          not own or have written permission to test.

4.3 REVOCATION. The research grant may be revoked at any time
    by the Authors. Upon revocation, all copies obtained under
    this Section must be destroyed within seven (7) days, except
    to the extent they form part of a published work already
    in the public record.

